{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>They spun the goats.</b> From upon the goats, as the Sages stated of blessed memory (Shabbat 99b), so that there would be added brilliance through the spinning — for in many materials, some of the excellence of their quality diminishes when they are uprooted from their place of growth, as happens with bees' honey and cassia and milk and the like."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {0 "קאסיא\"ה is a transliterated form (likely from Arabic/Greek) for cassia; read as such. זולתם rendered as 'and the like' (i.e., other similar substances)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:28:16.551160260Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}